    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "title": "Practical tip",
      "text": "Reset application state per test; use an isolated test database and dependency override when testing database routes."
    },
    {
      "type": "detail",
      "title": "One level deeper",
      "text": "`TestClient` lets synchronous tests exercise HTTP behavior; replacing external services with fakes keeps tests fast and reliable."
    },
    {
      "type": "warning",
      "title": "Important warning",
      "text": "Tests should not use real user data or a production database; use isolated state that can be reset."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUICK RECALL\n",
      "size": 20,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Question: Which action best prevents the common mistake from this lesson?\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Answer: Reset application state per test; use an isolated test database and dependency override when testing database routes.\n\n",
